IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `eia-core`
IMPORT `er4-nouns`

-- Employment Insurance Regulations (SOR/96-332), PART III.1, Division 4 Premium And Adjustment Payments -- Provincial
-- Plans and Division 5 Administrative Matters: regs 76.24 to 76.3. Layer 1 (the law, objectively), piece er4. Unofficial
-- plain-text rendering; nothing here is "verified against the official text". No section GIVEN.
--
-- THE RELATIONS. An employer deducts the employee's premium and remits the employer's premium under Act s 82(1) (out of
-- range, piece ei3). Whether the provincial premium reduction is taken into account at source depends on where the insured
-- person is employed and whether the provincial plan covers them (76.24, 76.25). The Minister of National Revenue pays a
-- province a premium adjustment for insured persons covered by its plan but employed elsewhere (76.26); what a person
-- overpaid is counted with that adjustment (76.28). The person's social insurance number is used to exchange information
-- with the province (76.29), which the Agency and the Minister may disclose (76.3).
-- Money is a NUMBER of dollars.

§ `Regulations 76.24 and 76.25 -- the premium reduction at source`

-- src:1284 | 76.24 Where an insured person who is covered by a provincial plan is employed by an employer in a province that has no provincial plan or is employed outside Canada, the employer shall not take into account any premium reduction for the purpose of
-- src:1285 | (a) deducting the amount required to be deducted as or on account of the employee’s premiums by paragraph 82(1)(a) of the Act; or
-- src:1286 | (b) remitting the amount of the employer’s premium required to be remitted in respect of that employee by paragraph 82(1)(b) of the Act.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 76.24 (src:1284-1286)
DECLARE `er4 Where the insured person is employed` IS ONE OF
    `er4 in a province that has a provincial plan`
    `er4 in a province that has no provincial plan`
    `er4 outside Canada`

-- The employer "shall not take into account any premium reduction" in deducting the employee's premium or remitting the
-- employer's premium, for a person covered by a provincial plan who is employed in a province with no plan or outside Canada.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 76.24 (src:1284-1286)
GIVEN `the insured person is covered by a provincial plan` IS A BOOLEAN
      employed IS A `er4 Where the insured person is employed`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 76.24 the employer is not to take any premium reduction into account in deducting the employee's premium or remitting the employer's premium` IF
        `the insured person is covered by a provincial plan`
    AND (employed EQUALS `er4 in a province that has no provincial plan` OR employed EQUALS `er4 outside Canada`)

-- src:1289 | 76.25 Where an insured person is employed by an employer in a province that has a provincial plan and the insured person is not covered by that plan, the employer shall take into account any premium reduction for the purpose of
-- src:1290 | (a) deducting the amount required to be deducted as or on account of the employee’s premiums by paragraph 82(1)(a) of the Act; and
-- src:1291 | (b) remitting the amount of the employer’s premium required to be remitted in respect of that employee by paragraph 82(1)(b) of the Act.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 76.25 (src:1289-1291)
GIVEN `the insured person is covered by the provincial plan` IS A BOOLEAN
      employed IS A `er4 Where the insured person is employed`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 76.25 the employer is to take any premium reduction into account in deducting the employee's premium and remitting the employer's premium` IF
        employed EQUALS `er4 in a province that has a provincial plan`
    AND (NOT `the insured person is covered by the provincial plan`)

§ `Regulation 76.26 -- the premium adjustment paid to a province`

-- src:1294 | 76.26 (1) The Minister of National Revenue shall pay to a province that has a provincial plan a premium adjustment consisting of the aggregate of :
-- src:1295 | (a) the amount obtained by adding together, for all insured persons referred to in section 76.24 who reside in that province on December 31 of a year, the amounts calculated in respect of each such insured person that represent the lesser of
-- src:1296 | (i) the total of
-- src:1297 | (A) all amounts that are deducted by employers in that year and that represent the premium reduction, as or on account of employee’s premiums, for the insured person, and
-- src:1298 | (B) all amounts representing an overpayment of employee’s premiums under Part IV of the Act in respect of the insured person for that year, and
-- src:1299 | (ii) all amounts that the insured person owes in that year under the provincial plan, and
-- src:1300 | (b) the total of all amounts that represent the premium reduction and that are remitted by employers in that year as employer’s premiums for every insured person referred to in section 76.24 who resides in that province on December 31 of that year.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 76.26(1) (src:1294-1300)
DECLARE `er4 Insured person referred to in section 76.24` HAS
    `er4 resides in the province on December 31 of the year`                                                       IS A BOOLEAN
    `er4 amounts deducted by employers in the year that represent the premium reduction, as or on account of employee's premiums`   IS A NUMBER   -- (a)(i)(A)
    `er4 amounts representing an overpayment of employee's premiums under Part IV of the Act for the year`          IS A NUMBER   -- (a)(i)(B)
    `er4 amounts the insured person owes in the year under the provincial plan`                                     IS A NUMBER   -- (a)(ii)
    `er4 amounts representing the premium reduction remitted by employers in the year as employer's premiums`      IS A NUMBER   -- (b)

-- The lesser of (i), the total of (A) and (B), and (ii), what the person owes under the provincial plan, for one person.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 76.26(1)(a) (src:1295-1299)
GIVEN person IS A `er4 Insured person referred to in section 76.24`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`reg 76.26(1)(a) the lesser of the total of the premium reduction deducted and the overpayment, and what the person owes under the provincial plan` MEANS
    min (person's `er4 amounts deducted by employers in the year that represent the premium reduction, as or on account of employee's premiums`
            PLUS person's `er4 amounts representing an overpayment of employee's premiums under Part IV of the Act for the year`)
        (person's `er4 amounts the insured person owes in the year under the provincial plan`)

-- (a): added together for all insured persons referred to in 76.24 "who reside in that province on December 31 of a year".
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 76.26(1)(a) (src:1295-1299)
GIVEN persons IS A LIST OF `er4 Insured person referred to in section 76.24`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`reg 76.26(1)(a) the amount obtained by adding together the amounts for the insured persons who reside in the province on December 31` MEANS
    sum (map `reg 76.26(1)(a) the lesser of the total of the premium reduction deducted and the overpayment, and what the person owes under the provincial plan`
             (filter (GIVEN p YIELD p's `er4 resides in the province on December 31 of the year`) persons))

-- src:1300 | (b) the total of all amounts that represent the premium reduction and that are remitted by employers in that year as employer’s premiums for every insured person referred to in section 76.24 who resides in that province on December 31 of that year.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 76.26(1)(b) (src:1300)
GIVEN persons IS A LIST OF `er4 Insured person referred to in section 76.24`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`reg 76.26(1)(b) the total of the premium reduction remitted by employers as employer's premiums for the insured persons who reside in the province on December 31` MEANS
    sum (map (GIVEN p YIELD p's `er4 amounts representing the premium reduction remitted by employers in the year as employer's premiums`)
             (filter (GIVEN p YIELD p's `er4 resides in the province on December 31 of the year`) persons))

@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 76.26(1) (src:1294-1300)
GIVEN persons IS A LIST OF `er4 Insured person referred to in section 76.24`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`reg 76.26(1) the premium adjustment that the Minister of National Revenue is to pay to the province` MEANS
    `reg 76.26(1)(a) the amount obtained by adding together the amounts for the insured persons who reside in the province on December 31` persons
        PLUS `reg 76.26(1)(b) the total of the premium reduction remitted by employers as employer's premiums for the insured persons who reside in the province on December 31` persons

§ `Regulation 76.28 -- overpayment and refund of the employee's premiums`

-- The premium adjustment the province has paid or must pay for premiums deducted under its plan is counted as though paid
-- on account of the employee's premiums under the Act, in deciding whether the employee overpaid (Act Part IV, out of
-- range, piece ei3); the rule gives the amount that is taken into account, not the overpayment itself.
-- src:1310 | 76.28 (1) If a province that has a provincial plan has paid or is required to pay to the Receiver General a premium adjustment that corresponds to the amount of employee’s premiums deducted in respect of an employee under that plan, that amount shall be taken into account as though the amount of the premium adjustment had been paid on account of the employee’s premiums under the Act for the purpose of determining whether there has been an overpayment by the employee for the purposes of Part IV of the Act.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 76.28(1) (src:1310)
GIVEN `the employee's premiums deducted and paid under the Act` IS A NUMBER
      `the premium adjustment that the province has paid or is required to pay to the Receiver General and that corresponds to the employee's premiums deducted under the provincial plan` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`reg 76.28(1) the employee's premiums taken into account in determining whether there has been an overpayment` MEANS
    `the employee's premiums deducted and paid under the Act`
        PLUS `the premium adjustment that the province has paid or is required to pay to the Receiver General and that corresponds to the employee's premiums deducted under the provincial plan`

-- src:1311 | (2) Where a premium adjustment referred to in subsection 76.26(1) has been paid or is required to be paid to a province that has a provincial plan, the amount of that premium adjustment shall not be taken into account for the purposes of Part IV of the Act.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 76.28(2) (src:1311)
GIVEN `the amount is a premium adjustment referred to in subsection 76.26(1) that has been paid or is required to be paid to a province that has a provincial plan` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 76.28(2) the amount is taken into account for the purposes of Part IV of the Act` IF
    NOT `the amount is a premium adjustment referred to in subsection 76.26(1) that has been paid or is required to be paid to a province that has a provincial plan`

§ `Regulations 76.29 and 76.3 -- administrative matters`

-- src:1316 | 76.29 A claimant’s social insurance number shall be used for the purpose of facilitating the exchange, between the Government of Canada and a province, of information obtained with respect to a claimant under provincial law or the Act.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 76.29 (src:1316)
GIVEN `the use is for the purpose of facilitating the exchange, between the Government of Canada and a province, of information obtained with respect to the claimant under provincial law or the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 76.29 the claimant's social insurance number is to be used` IF
    `the use is for the purpose of facilitating the exchange, between the Government of Canada and a province, of information obtained with respect to the claimant under provincial law or the Act`

-- src:1319 | 76.3 The Canada Revenue Agency and the Minister of National Revenue are authorized to disclose to a province that has a provincial plan information necessary for the administration of this Part that has been obtained by the Agency or the Minister under the Act or these Regulations and any information prepared from that information.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 76.3 (src:1319)
GIVEN `the province has a provincial plan` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the information is necessary for the administration of this Part` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the information was obtained by the Agency or the Minister under the Act or these Regulations, or was prepared from information so obtained` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 76.3 the Canada Revenue Agency and the Minister of National Revenue are authorized to disclose the information to the province` IF
        `the province has a provincial plan`
    AND `the information is necessary for the administration of this Part`
    AND `the information was obtained by the Agency or the Minister under the Act or these Regulations, or was prepared from information so obtained`
